(Hamamatsu S360 | Color jitter | epoch 3 | 0.700 | 0.207 | 0.761 | 0.326) Tj
T*
(Hamammatsu XR | Baseline | epoch 3 | 0.700 | 0.623 | 0.491 | 0.550) Tj
T*
(Hamammatsu XR | Color jitter | epoch 3 | 0.700 | 0.596 | 0.669 | 0.630) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Mean best-checkpoint results:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Model | Mean Precision | Mean Recall | Mean F1) Tj
T*
(Baseline | 0.580 | 0.598 | 0.581) Tj
T*
(Color jitter | 0.469 | 0.719 | 0.539) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(9. Interpretation) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The patch-level experiment suggested that color augmentation can improve scanner) Tj
T*
(generalization, especially recall. The full detection experiment showed a more complicated) Tj
T*
(but more realistic picture.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Key findings:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Checkpoint choice matters. Several final checkpoints were worse than earlier checkpoints.) Tj
T*
(This suggests training instability and possible overfitting.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Color jitter increased recall overall. The color-jitter detector had mean recall 0.719) Tj
T*
(compared with 0.598 for the baseline. This means it found more true mitotic figures.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Color jitter reduced precision overall. The color-jitter detector had mean precision) Tj
T*
(0.469 compared with 0.580 for the baseline. This means it produced more false positives.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. Color jitter helped some scanner holdouts but hurt others. It improved Aperio CS2 and) Tj
T*
(Hamammatsu XR, but performed poorly on Hamamatsu S360.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. Hamamatsu S360 appears to be a difficult or mismatched scanner domain for the current) Tj
T*
(augmentation approach. The S360 color-jitter model had high recall but many false positives,) Tj
T*
(which caused low F1.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(10. Current Conclusion) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The current results support the broader project idea that scanner appearance affects mitosis) Tj
T*
(detection performance. However, simple color jitter is not a complete solution.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The strongest current conclusion is:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Scanner generalization is sensitive to both augmentation strategy and training stability.) Tj
T*
(Color augmentation can improve recall and help some held-out scanner domains, but it can) Tj
T*
(also increase false positives and reduce F1 if the augmentation does not match the held-out) Tj
T*
(scanner distribution.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F1 8 Tf
